  "prompt": "Construct a quasigroup of order 12 satisfying QG3 idempotence and the involution property. Specifically: an n\u00d7n grid x with values in {0, ..., 11} such that:\n  - Every row and every column is a permutation of 0..11 (Latin square)\n  - x[i][i] = i for all i in [0, 12) (idempotent diagonal)\n  - x[ x[i][j] ][ x[j][i] ] = i for all i, j in [0, 12) (QG3)\nThe third constraint involves nested indexing (the indices themselves are values from x). For n in [5, 12], few solutions exist and search is non-trivial.\n\nReturn the grid as a flat list of 144 integers in row-major order (cell (i,j) at index i*12+j), or state \"UNSATISFIABLE\".",
